# Capability-triggered domain checks 0.1

Revision `sop-rules-addendum-20261016-0.1`. This English reference follows the [original Chinese domain checks](../规范补充-20261016/领域检查.md). Screen scope using [applicability and version](applicability-and-version.md). Each row specifies document design and future verification. Actual claims require evidence from the applicable project.

| ID and trigger facts | Product requirements | Technical design | Counterexamples and required evidence | Related original rules |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| DOM01 Accessibility. A user interface or promised assistive access exists. | Specify how users perform and read core tasks. Cover names, errors, status feedback, required keyboard order, focus, zoom or reflow, and cues beyond color. Explain restrictions and available alternatives. | Define platform semantics and names, roles, and states. Specify focus restoration, keyboard exit, and status announcements. Verify platform-specific constraints. | Complete the core task using only the keyboard. Verify that focus remains visible and can leave controls, that users can locate and correct errors, and that users perceive dynamic status. Record actual operation on the required platforms and assistive technology. Claims of WCAG conformance require evidence beyond visual review. | PC05/PC06/PC11/PC12, TC08/TC12/TC13 |
| DOM02 Concurrency and consistency. Shared resources, multiple users or windows, background and foreground writes, or repeated side effects exist. | Define who can succeed in a conflict and what others see. Specify whether overwrite, merge, queue, or rejection is allowed. Identify invariants such as a single available slot or available inventory. | Define authoritative writes, atomic commit boundaries, expected revisions and conflict responses, idempotency key scope and lifetime, same key with a different payload, ordering, partial completion, and unknown outcomes. Address permission revocation between a read and a dependent action. | Two requests for the same resource must preserve the invariant. Reject stale writes or merge under the confirmed policy. Retry without duplicate commits. Check current state after a network disconnect. Record the interleaving, final durable state, and side effects. | PC08/PC09/PC14, TC03/TC04/TC05/TC06, KB11/KB16, SEC02/SEC11, TASK09 |
