## Adoption depth and design handoff

Identify the object and the applicability basis and substantiate every current required condition. Reuse R/J/F/BR/MOD/API/DATA/T/AC/E/ISS IDs and the authoritative text. Describe user behavior in product design, guarantees and boundaries in technical design, implementation and verification in tasks, and levels and gaps in the review card.

Select files, services, infrastructure, and L3 depth according to project consequences. Document design can proceed with key hypotheses marked for verification and their dependent work blocked. An applicable check remains required if it fails. Reuse evidence according to its content and version bindings. Record uncompiled domains with CUSTOM IDs and retain the frozen checks' own results.

## External methods and limits

The original supplement records the reading below on 2026-10-16. Its method notes retain the reading scope for dynamic pages. FormSy designed the DOM IDs, fields, triggers, statuses, and counterexamples.

- The source records reading the abstract, contents, and keyboard, focus, errors, status messages, and conformance sections. These sections inform testable accessibility constraints and review of the complete task. Conformance assessment and selection of an AA requirement depend on the applicable project. [W3C WCAG 2.2, Recommendation of 2024-12-12](https://www.w3.org/TR/2024/REC-WCAG22-20241212/)
- The source records reading §§1, 3 and 3.1, and 3.4 on timestamps, additional time-zone information, and offset consistency. Apply those distinctions when designing time behavior. The project owns scheduling conflict, recurrence, catch-up, and timeout policies. [RFC 9557](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9557.html)
- The source records reading relevant sections on checklist adaptation, maintenance, reliability, and recovery. Scale actionable checks to project risk. Staffing processes and service-level targets depend on the project. [Google SRE, Reliable Product Launches](https://sre.google/sre-book/reliable-product-launches/)

The concurrency, notification, privacy, AI, and payment additions primarily follow existing local rules and this design. Establish actual jurisdiction, platform, service facts, and obligations with applicable primary sources for the project.
